{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar","id":1280838,"title":"What\u2019s the over/under on Warstrider Solar vs Daikaiju Lunar?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-14T23:33:59-08:00","id":1280838,"title":"What\u2019s the over/under on Warstrider Solar vs Daikaiju Lunar?","content":"Now, mea culpa I have not done a deep dive of the Warstrider rules in AOTC, hence why I am turning to you, my learned compatriots.<br /> <br /> Is the free use of all Charms (sans MA since you have to be in animal shape I suppose) equal in any fashion to Warstrider evocations and artifact weapons? <br /> <br /> Or does the Solar basically auto-win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-15-2019, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T23:37:26-08:00","id":1280840,"title":"","content":"Nobody auto-wins a fight in Ex3 excepting a massively one-sided fight or trivial opponents and such. The tactics you use can make or break a fight.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Solar still generally has to have a pretty high Essence score to get to the more devastating warstrider Evocations. For instance, an Essence 1 Solar climbing into Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation won't have access to its reality-stabilizing cannonade or its implosion bow or lightning ballista, or even its targeting systems. Plus he's gotta power it with a hearthstone.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlus, we don't have the rules for Lunars yet. That seems like an important factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-15-2019, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T00:42:53-08:00","id":1280848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar#post1280838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the free use of all Charms (sans MA since you have to be in animal shape I suppose) equal in any fashion Warstrider evocations and artifact weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Solar in the warstrider will also be able to freely use most of their Charms.<br /> <br /> It's really hard to effectively assess this match up, considering that we only have a full enough picture of one side of it. We don't really know what the capabilities and constraints of the Lunar that goes really big are.<br /> <br /> Mind, I have a feeling that when a Lunar faces a warstrider, their best bet is in going small rather than big; turn into something that the warstrider can barely hit, and then go for the gambits to break down its limbs and the like, rather than matching power for power.<br /> <br /> Still, that may depend on the build of the Lunar. Will it be possible to equip with capabilities that extend or complement a gigantic shape, a deep investment in which will make it advantageous against warstriders and behemoths? Iuhuh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T00:53:59-08:00","id":1280849,"title":"","content":"Right - much easier to slip through the warstrider's fuselage as a mouse and then terrorize the strapped-in pilot inside as a tiger, than to just stand outside the thing and trade blows. .<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T02:19:14-08:00","id":1280862,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I was ready to make a comment about it seeming as though, barring certain additional powers, going huge to fight a huge thing would hardly ever be advantageous, but then realized I wasn't giving due consideration to the benefits of Legendary Size, and mitigating them through having a similar size.<br /> <br /> That's how that works, right? I'll check my book later.<br /> <br /> It's a bit different for warstriders, since they're uniformly vulnerable to gambits to lower their function and mobility, and even expose the vulnerable pilot.<br /> <br /> Still and all, the right combination of Strength and Stamina Charms with Protean enhancements to a huge size... I'm more readily imagining how it could give a Solar in a warstrider a run for their money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T02:42:44-08:00","id":1280865,"title":"","content":"Here\u2019s my logic for asking:<br /> <br /> 1. While I am behind on Warstrider news, I have devoured any scrap of Lunars info out there. Being able to Daikaiju is one of the coolest things they can do E1, so I thought I\u2019d ask.<br /> <br /> 2. If going all Pacific Rim is the wrong way to defeat giant robots, I don\u2019t want to be right (yes I know all the monsters in Pacific Rim got killed by hidden chain swords). <br /> <br /> 3. There is a part of me that wonders (as Isator) if there is anything in the Lunar Charmset that lets them keep up with Warstrider Evocations at higher essence other than \u201cDaikaiju form becomes basically free to maintain\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T02:45:21-08:00","id":1280866,"title":"","content":"I mean, <i>every</i> splat gets something to keep up with Evocations at high Essence. They're called Charms. Between a Melee Supernal Solar and a guy in a warstrider, I wouldn't count out the Melee Supernal Solar very quickly, and likewise, I wouldn't put it past an Essence 5 Lunar to block a warstrider's punch bare-handed and then wrench the arm out of its socket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-15-2019, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T03:19:51-08:00","id":1280868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280865#post1280865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. While I am behind on Warstrider news, I have devoured any scrap of Lunars info out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that one of those is free, but Arms of the Chosen is still out there to make one of those more concrete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If going all Pacific Rim is the wrong way to defeat giant robots, I don\u2019t want to be right</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I meant to acknowledge the significance of temperament of character and player, and how one approach shouldn't be strictly inferior even if its main appeal was cosmetic (which it probably won't be).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. There is a part of me that wonders (as Isator) if there is anything in the Lunar Charmset that lets them keep up with Warstrider Evocations at higher essence other than \u201cDaikaiju form becomes basically free to maintain\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really what I'm wondering, but... What's the metric for &quot;keeping up&quot;?<br /> <br /> For that matter, it depends a bit on the warstrider in question; a Lunar will probably never really match the upper reach of Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation's long range destructive saturation, but outfighting that one in single combat isn't the most difficult proposition. Other noble warstriders get more specific, where it becomes a simple case of &quot;these just aren't Lunar powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> For royal warstriders... on the one hand, they're Artifact N/A, by definition they have enormous power the likes of which the Exalted are hard pressed to match. On the other, while the Walking Devil Tower has the power to erase things from existence, you don't really need an equivalent to beat it into the ground.<br /> <br /> Be mindful of how the power of warstriders is often expressed in ways other than how hard they hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T03:40:16-08:00","id":1280869,"title":"","content":"as someone who hasn't kept up with the spoilers, I need to ask: can Lunars do Kaiju this edistion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T03:45:49-08:00","id":1280870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280869#post1280869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as someone who hasn't kept up with the spoilers, I need to ask: can Lunars do Kaiju this edistion?</div> </div> </div> </div>From Character Creation even! But it basically takes a whole bunch of motes and your entire mote drip each round to maintain. At higher essence (3 or 4...?) it becomes free to maintain with an upgrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T04:57:43-08:00","id":1280877,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, what's been said is that Lunars can assume an animal form with Legendary Size. The Legendary Size animals from the Core are armored terrors, emperor sloths, ox-dragons, river dragons, siege lizards, tyrant lizards, and yeddim.<br /> <br /> So more Jurassic Park than Godzilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-15-2019, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T05:14:48-08:00","id":1280879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280877#post1280877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, what's been said is that Lunars can assume an animal form with Legendary Size. The Legendary Size animals from the Core are armored terrors, emperor sloths, ox-dragons, river dragons, siege lizards, tyrant lizards, and yeddim.<br /> <br /> So more Jurassic Park than Godzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>And warstriders are Guymelef size instead of EVA-01 size too. So they tie pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T05:52:50-08:00","id":1280883,"title":"","content":"The solar wins.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why we're supposed to be so coy about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T07:14:05-08:00","id":1280896,"title":"","content":"Yea like if you took a dawn caste and told them to fight a full moon that fights as a dino they are going to win hands down every time. Giving them a warstrider is just overkill.<br /> Edit: Like the whole reason you would want to spend the insane mote cost on turning into a legendary size creature as a lunar is to get the legendary size merit.<br /> <br /> Giving the Solar a Warstrider negates any benefit from that merit and gives them access to a spectacular set of abilities at a fraction of the cost. In a white room fight the only way the lunar wins this is if they have a massive essence advantage and the solar has like melee 3 with no charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","user":"Calboon","date":". 01-15-2019, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T09:05:19-08:00","id":1280913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280877#post1280877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, what's been said is that Lunars can assume an animal form with Legendary Size. The Legendary Size animals from the Core are armored terrors, emperor sloths, ox-dragons, river dragons, siege lizards, tyrant lizards, and yeddim.<br /> <br /> So more Jurassic Park than Godzilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to note that Emperor Ox Expansion also fell way short of Godzilla and that Legendary Size gives you more of a bonus for being large and powerful than it ever did. Speaking, as someone who was horribly disapointed with it last edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T10:11:32-08:00","id":1280927,"title":"","content":"A thirty foot Lunar vs. a thirty foot Solar is approximately just a Lunar vs. a Solar so the answer is the usual one: all else equal the Solar has the advantage, but all else is pretty rarely equal. Of course in this case one of the unequal all-elses is heavily in the Lunar\u2019s disfavor, namely having their mote recovery slashed 80% without a higher-Essence upgrade/repurchase(?), but that\u2019s the price you pay for not having to drag a warstrider to the dramatic mountaintop arena where I assume this fight is happening and (much more importantly for this purpose) not needing Resources 4 to heal up for round two. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T11:22:58-08:00","id":1280944,"title":"","content":"The main advantages of the warstrider are as follows:<br /> <br /> \u200b1) Truly awesome Evocations.<br /> \u200b2) Legendary Size bonus/mitigating the bonuses of a Legendary Size opponent.<br /> 3) The free Devastate action each turn.<br /> \u200b4) Having a whole second health track, plus the warstrider's Soak and Hardness.<br /> 5) The warstrider's weapons are artifact weapons.<br /> \u200b6) Sheer awesome factor.<br /> <br /> The main disadvantages of the warstrider are as follows:<br /> <br /> \u200b1) Huge Merit cost. The lowest-costed ones are still five dots, <i>plus</i> you need to power it with a hearthstone.<br /> \u200b2) Huge mote cost that could go toward powering combat Charms.<br /> \u200b3) Fighting human-scale opponents gets a -4 dice penalty. There's a further -3 penalty if you're not specifically trained to fight in a warstrider.<br /> \u200b4) It's vulnerable to gambits that disable its limbs or block its vision or breach its fuselage in a way that leaves the pilot vulnerable.<br /> \u200b5) There's not a single warstrider Evocation available at Essence 1.<br /> 6) Maintenance and repair.<br /> <br /> So again, you can't just toss <i>any </i>warstrider at <i>any </i>Dawn and say, &quot;There, now he wins.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-15-2019, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T11:33:41-08:00","id":1280947,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't realize that we had some Lunar playtesters here, who have evidently given some <i>very</i> harsh feedback on the document.<br /> <br /> Still, here's hoping that there's time and energy to make adjustments in the correct direction based on their insights, lest Lunar fans be disappointed for yet another Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T12:48:17-08:00","id":1280961,"title":"","content":"My feeling about how it <i>should </i>work is that it depends entirely on their age, experience, Caste, specialization of strengths chosen, circumstances of the battle, and whether the Lunar is rocking any significant artefact of their own of a comparable grandeur and puissance to the Warstrider! (Plus luck).<br /> <br /> I'd say Warstriders should be certainly be great for offsetting the disadvantages faced by being a small scale fighter trying to battle something big... <br /> <br /> So if you're playing a Solar who totally doesn't have any other way of fighting something big, and is really focused on human scale opponents, a warstrider might be an efficient way to scale up and offset your disadvantage.<br /> <br /> But Solars should have loads of other ways they can draw to tackle big monsters on even if they don't have a Warstrider - ranged, athletics (lots of leaping and clambering), sorcery, evocations, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T12:56:02-08:00","id":1280962,"title":"","content":"I specifically asked the devs if a Lunar could become a giant human or beastfolk instead of just an animal.<br /> <br /> They confirmed that Lunars could.<br /> <br /> So a Lunar could Ultraman / Eren Yager it up to use Martial Arts and handheld weapons at giant sizes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T13:10:00-08:00","id":1280966,"title":"","content":"I was counting humans as animals in that post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T14:46:45-08:00","id":1280983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280865#post1280865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here\u2019s my logic for asking:<br /> <br /> 1. While I am behind on Warstrider news, I have devoured any scrap of Lunars info out there. Being able to Daikaiju is one of the coolest things they can do E1, so I thought I\u2019d ask.<br /> <br /> 2. If going all Pacific Rim is the wrong way to defeat giant robots, I don\u2019t want to be right (yes I know all the monsters in Pacific Rim got killed by hidden chain swords).<br /> <br /> 3. There is a part of me that wonders (as Isator) if there is anything in the Lunar Charmset that lets them keep up with Warstrider Evocations at higher essence other than \u201cDaikaiju form becomes basically free to maintain\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>This question would be a lot easier to answer if we were talking about Lunar in a warstrider vs Daikaiju Lunar. Also this could vary wildly depending on the Solar and Lunar in question, and even a solid streak of luck, but I'm taking it as understood that we're talking about two opponents similarly matched against their peers. I'm not assuming what happens when a meek bureaucrat Solar jumps into a strider to fight a hardened and vicious veteran of a hundred wars.<br /> <br /> If we're assuming equal essence here, and I imagine turning into a kaiju is not a low essence Lunar effect, then Solars just have too much going for them. At low essence the attunement cost might be too much to deal with, but even at essence 3 it starts to ease up a lot more. At that point the Solar will have access to things like Adamant Skin Technique, Ox-Stunning Blow's essence 3 upgrade, and Hungry Tiger Technique even if they're not in supernal, and as a combat supernal they'll have all that plus the capstones of that ability.<br /> <br /> A Lunar in giant monster form will be quite powerful indeed, but not in the right ways to give them an edge against a Solar, particularly since things like legendary size are not applicable to warstriders. They edge they'll get for being giant monster is more like smashing through castles and armies, not defeating monster-slaying heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T18:09:29-08:00","id":1281016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280962#post1280962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I specifically asked the devs if a Lunar could become a giant human or beastfolk instead of just an animal.<br /> <br /> They confirmed that Lunars could.<br /> <br /> So a Lunar could Ultraman / Eren Yager it up to use Martial Arts and handheld weapons at giant sizes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! So it can be Kung Fu Kaiju Lunar vs Warstrider! Fantastic! (for those who don\u2019t know Lunars can mix native charms freely with Martial Arts ones).<br /> <br /> Well, whoever wins in the end, that\u2019s a good fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T20:46:44-08:00","id":1281037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1280983#post1280983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This question would be a lot easier to answer if we were talking about Lunar in a warstrider vs Daikaiju Lunar. Also this could vary wildly depending on the Solar and Lunar in question, and even a solid streak of luck, but I'm taking it as understood that we're talking about two opponents similarly matched against their peers. I'm not assuming what happens when a meek bureaucrat Solar jumps into a strider to fight a hardened and vicious veteran of a hundred wars.<br /> <br /> If we're assuming equal essence here, and I imagine turning into a kaiju is not a low essence Lunar effect, then Solars just have too much going for them. At low essence the attunement cost might be too much to deal with, but even at essence 3 it starts to ease up a lot more. At that point the Solar will have access to things like Adamant Skin Technique, Ox-Stunning Blow's essence 3 upgrade, and Hungry Tiger Technique even if they're not in supernal, and as a combat supernal they'll have all that plus the capstones of that ability.<br /> <br /> A Lunar in giant monster form will be quite powerful indeed, but not in the right ways to give them an edge against a Solar, particularly since things like legendary size are not applicable to warstriders. They edge they'll get for being giant monster is more like smashing through castles and armies, not defeating monster-slaying heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, as far as I can gather, Kaiju is a character creation achieveable ability. It\u2019s not high essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-15T22:26:53-08:00","id":1281044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281037#post1281037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, as far as I can gather, Kaiju is a character creation achieveable ability. It\u2019s not high essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar might be able to get an edge at essence 1 or around there then, it's still hard though. Even a weaker warstrider costs 15m to attune to, 4 more than an artifact weapon and armour. For those 4 extra motes you get to ignore legendary size, have your strength set to probably 7, or 6 if you went more into stamina, and get 30 health levels as an overshield on the warstrider. Never mind the evocations that bonus strength, durability, and disabling one of the most powerful features of your giant opponent is totally worth it. Now factor in that if you're going Full-Moon vs Dawn that Dawn is going to have a supernal combat ability, so they might have up to essence 5 combat charms anyway, and will likely have a bigger mote pool to start. <br /> <br /> Basically as a Lunar you're already starting behind your Solar opponent due to the power differences, and attuning to a warstrider is almost the best thing to spend your motes on when fighting a giant monster. In fact unless you're trying to pull off some 40 mote instant kill Solar doom combo on turn one it probably is strictly the best thing to invest motes in.<br /> <br /> The real key to feeling like a powerful exalt is don't compare yourself to a similarly invested Solar, lol.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also when I say an edge I do mean, like, an edge. It's not some insurmountable task, it's just if you and I both roll d20s and I have +1 to the roll I have the advantage. Tactics or specific builds or luck can swing it easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-16-2019, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T00:50:39-08:00","id":1281056,"title":"","content":"I feel as though, of all the Exalted (and most other beings besides), a Lunar Exalt of the Full Moon Caste will be the most able to get reasonably close to a Dawn Caste Solar of... roughly the same level of development, accounting from the difficult to compare things like Supernal Ability and a library of shapes, as well as the somewhat broader array of capabilities per Attribute.<br /> <br /> I would propose that a Full Moon who cleverly applies the advantages of things like moving between multiple shapes (for which they've got good Protean Charms), capabilities that the Solar can't exactly have on their own (such as generating poisons and the presumably still highly potent regeneration), and whatever the anima powers are, that should be a Lunar who has a decent chance of overcoming a fighting Solar.<br /> <br /> I previously realised that a Lunar in large form probably still has advantages, but also think that a Lunar who sticks to one form the entire fight is not entirely playing to their strengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T01:06:32-08:00","id":1281058,"title":"","content":"Yeah, agreed. Also there's just really obvious ones like a Solar battling a mega-shark Lunar in the middle of a storm tossed sea at night. At that Solar is spending motes on dipping swallow or the like every turn just to not have their defence pool dropped by -5 every attack. Or Element Resisting Prana but that's an essence 3 survival charm so what are the chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T03:02:13-08:00","id":1281068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281056#post1281056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I previously realised that a Lunar in large form probably still has advantages, but also think that a Lunar who sticks to one form the entire fight is not entirely playing to their strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're certainly the most constrained in their options by the original post, it's probably most advantageous for the Lunar to start in a normal-sized or even tiny form and exploit the Limitations of Scale rule to force the Solar to waste precious essence.<br /> <br /> Another factor I see here is that if the Warstrider has poor long-ranged capability and can't fly, since that would allow the Lunar to call timeout almost whenever they want. If they've got something that passively heals them over the course of several rounds, this could allow them to trade the Solar blow for blow before going to a relatively safe distance to heal up and try again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T07:56:54-08:00","id":1281096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281068#post1281068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another factor I see here is that if the Warstrider has poor long-ranged capability and can't fly, since that would allow the Lunar to call timeout almost whenever they want. If they've got something that passively heals them over the course of several rounds, this could allow them to trade the Solar blow for blow before going to a relatively safe distance to heal up and try again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or burrow. I'm suddenly seeing a Lunar taking cues from The Sword in the Stone, who turns into a vole to burrow down as if to hide, and while the warstrider digs for them they've already emerged elsewhere to prepare an attack from behind.<br /> <br /> Hell, with a mildly accomodating Storyteller, a Lunar could conceivably hide inside of the warstrider itself.<br /> <br /> Or get inside the fuselage as something annoying, even dangerous. I don't care how much somebody affords a Solar in theorycraft or how good their Melee is, given how piloting a warstrider works in game mechanics, if a rodent is biting at you with sharp little teeth while your limbs are strapped into a big heavy harness, your responses are a bit limited.<br /> <br /> Sure, some warstriders might have Iron Man-esque internal countermeasures, and less hardware in the interface. See my first response.<br /> <br /> And even with matching power for power, well: the first thing I think of with that is that the only thing a Lunar needs for a dice cap as good as a Solar's is a stunt. Sure sure, the XP and BP costs shake out a bit differently (although if Strength and Dexterity are both in caste...), but all things being equal, your Lunar can probably consistently hit a Solar (or threaten to hit enough to pull in costly defence), and even a warstrider's soak can't stop all of that (what kinds of armour piercing Charms will Lunars have?).<br /> <br /> There are probably things within the Solar combat suite that come out stronger than what Lunars can get. Free excellencies, say. Defenses that can go a bit further. Things that maintain the concept of Solars as the mightiest overall.<br /> <br /> But between what we've seen, what's been implied, and what we know of the abilities and leanings of these developers and writers, I think Lunars will get some formidable tricks of their own, enough to make such a theoretical bout an actual contest.<br /> <br /> I think something in their combat prowess can be seen in comparing Flowing Body Evasion to Seven Shadow Evasion and Heavenly Guardian Defence; its rate is more fixed, but it's also less costly. Is that a worse defense? I think that depends on how the fight goes, before and after (do you ever think a Solar saves their own life with Heavenly Guardian Defence, only to be crashed immediately after?)<br /> <br /> To simply declare that the Solar will just win is... <i>tediously</i> unimaginative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:20:09-08:00","id":1281216,"title":"","content":"Personally, were I the Lunar in this fight, I\u2019d be trying to keep aggro with the Solar while staying out of range of a big response and either lead it into a prepared trap, like a camouflaged giant pit of mud, or until the solar got far enough away from their support team that I could circle back and destroy their Warstrider maintenance supplies.<br /> <br /> Assuming I can pull that off, the Warstrider\u2019s advantages will be effectively negated and I can try a few different things to kill the Solar while they try to get the Warstrider set back up. Including driving a Tyrant Lizard through their camp at 5 am.<br /> <br /> Edit: And, yes, I get that people want to build Lunar Daikaju that are easily as scary as any of the Warstriders in Arms. I have no issue with that, it\u2019s just not my usual method of fighting. I will say that I\u2019m hopeful that such forms will be possible to create and I don\u2019t think the devs will disappoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 01-16-2019, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T17:44:24-08:00","id":1281221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281096#post1281096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To simply declare that the Solar will just win is... <i>tediously</i> unimaginative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is kind of directed at me, but I also think it is misplaced. The original post wanted to know how a kaiju form would stack up against a Solar in a warstrider, and it's not great. The combat benefits granted to a character by climbing into a warstrider are overwhelming, and Solars are already ahead of Lunars in power.. Kaiju form would have to provide something better than 30-55 free health levels, +3 strength, +2 to +5 speed bonus, in addition to Legendary Size. On the flip side a warstrider takes a -4 penalty to hit singular opponents that are human sized or smaller, and ignores any opponent's Legendary Size merit.<br /> <br /> It's not a foregone conclusion, but if you want to talk about Lunar Kaiju vs Dragonblooded in a warstrider that would be a MUCH better fight. Also it means that the first essence 1 athletics 1 charm doesn't make tactics like bogging them down in a pit of mud not-applicable. I don't think DBs actually have a charm anywhere that lets them run across a swamp without sinking in. THAT would be a damn good brawl, and I might put my money on the Lunar in that case.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also not sure if it's a GOOD thing that becoming a giant monster is not the best way for a Lunar to fight a Solar in a Warstrider, it might be for a DB in a Warstrider, not sure, but that's what the rules seem to play it out to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T18:58:24-08:00","id":1281235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281221#post1281221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this is kind of directed at me, but I also think it is misplaced.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it was directed at people whose answers were more boring. You, at least, engage with the topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The original post wanted to know how a kaiju form would stack up against a Solar in a warstrider, and it's not great. The combat benefits granted to a character by climbing into a warstrider are overwhelming, and Solars are already ahead of Lunars in power. </div> </div> </div>In what ways are the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation overwhelming? How far ahead are Solars? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kaiju form would have to provide something better than 30-55 free health levels, +3 strength, +2 to +5 speed bonus, in addition to Legendary Size. </div> </div> </div>What of Protean Charms?<br /> <br /> That being said, if the original (or any follow up) question was about whether a Lunar using their own Charms should be equivalent to another Exalt wielding an Artifact, I feel as though the answer should be of course not; that thing isn\u2019t just cosmetic, it\u2019s an additional source of distinct powers. Your shapeshifting ought not to be the equivalent of growing some Artifacts ad hoc.<br /> <br /> Mind, the scenario raises questions such as whether buying the Evocations left less XP to buy Solar Charms, or whether the Lunar has a size-changing suit of high level armour to draw similar power from.<br /> <br /> The defeatism raises its own questions, such as whether people think that opponents of Gorgon and Stormcaller are also helpless, or if they\u2019re proposing that the writers are aiming to create Lunars incapable of achieving the feats attributed to them in the more recent fiction. <br /> <br /> Is the hypothetical Solar going into battle wearing Karvara\u2019s corpse, perhaps?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also not sure if it's a GOOD thing that becoming a giant monster is not the best way for a Lunar to fight a Solar in a Warstrider </div> </div> </div>I think that \u201cbest\u201d may prove a more circumstantial thing.<br /> <br /> The other side of the coin is that warstriders aren\u2019t necessarily the best thing to fight lone demigods, rather than armies and giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T08:40:23-08:00","id":1281300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281216#post1281216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: And, yes, I get that people want to build Lunar Daikaju that are easily as scary as any of the Warstriders in Arms. I have no issue with that, it\u2019s just not my usual method of fighting. I will say that I\u2019m hopeful that such forms will be possible to create and I don\u2019t think the devs will disappoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Main issue I see the people who want Lunar Daikaju having is the loss of knacks like Heart's Theft of the Behemoth, though that's in the same category as Emperor Ox Expansion for being an overrated vanity power.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The problem with Heart's Theft of the Behemoth was that at essence 5 it was limited to behemoths no larger than a Tyrant Lizard. So once again, you couldn't be most versions of King Kong (and I'd argue that the Peter Jackson version isn't a behemoth so much as a rare animal). Within that range, most behemoths without their charms are less dangerous than a Tyrant Lizard. The only real merit was so you could show up to the next gathering as the Man-Hunting Gigaweasel as proof of your acomplishments. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I do have an idea for better capturing the behemoth form experience without wrecking the game but I need to Fangs at the Gate before I can figure out the fine details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T09:01:32-08:00","id":1281306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281216#post1281216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I get that people want to build Lunar Daikaju that are easily as scary as any of the Warstriders in Arms. I have no issue with that</div> </div> </div> </div>I bloody do; it\u2019s way too extreme.<br /> <br /> Maybe back in Second Edition, when all they were was some extra soak and Strength points, but now they do things that are actually interesting, another Exalt should not be equal without any of the investments. <br /> <br /> Perhaps as a hypothetical for Charms above Essence 5.<br /> <br /> The best that I would say is adding some advantages and reducing the gap in a similar manner to a Solar going super saiyan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T11:38:54-08:00","id":1281330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281306#post1281306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I bloody do; it\u2019s way too extreme.<br /> <br /> Maybe back in Second Edition, when all they were was some extra soak and Strength points, but now they do things that are actually interesting, another Exalt should not be equal without any of the investments. <br /> <br /> Perhaps as a hypothetical for Charms above Essence 5.<br /> <br /> The best that I would say is adding some advantages and reducing the gap in a similar manner to a Solar going super saiyan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I\u2019m not saying a starting Lunar should be able to become Deathbringer, The Mother of Crows, She Who Blots Out The Sun at chargen, but I expect the Daikaiju charm tree to be big enough and go into high enough essence that you can become a Mythic Beast from the Primordial War if you get all of it and I expect such creatures to be legitimately terrifying in similar ways to Warstriders.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I\u2019d want my ultimate E5 Daikaiju form to be at least somewhere on par with a Survival Supernal Solar\u2019s fully upgraded Familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T12:19:11-08:00","id":1281338,"title":"","content":"I played an Essence 5 Solar with Godspeed Vanguard and most of its evocations (and compatible Solar powers like some Melee, Athletics and Stealth charms).<br /> <br /> I used it in one fight; one where it wasn't really necessary, I just wanted to show off.<br /> <br /> The problem is they're just do damn awkward to get around. I had a charm+evocation that meant I was able to go at 100 mph, and specifically chose Godspeed Vanguard because it can do so (most Warstriders are slow; it's not like your sorcerer friend can carry you in his Stormwind Rider, or your Eclipse friend can carry you on his super-fast elephant), though I still had to invest in Athletics charms.<br /> 100 mph probabably doesn't seem so bad. But travelling can cause damage, so you don't want to travel much. And if you're sneaking somewhere, or going on a diplomatic mission, you can't take it with you. At least with artefact armour you can get a charm to keep it in elsewhere, but that's not possible with a Warstrider.<br /> <br /> Then there's the awkwardness of fixing them. To even be able to do so practically, you need a lot of investment in Craft. Even with that, I rarely had the time to fix it up, and it ended up covered in lava and thus needing a full repair, which I never had time for.<br /> And all that Craft really cut into my other abilities' charms.<br /> <br /> And then of course you need to buy the Warstrider (a level 5 artefact) and have a Greater Hearthstone (4 dots, 5 with a Manse) to power it.<br /> <br /> A Lunar though? They can fly as a small bird into the middle of the enemy camp and go full Kaiju. They can attend a decadent soiree at the Queen's palace, and then when demonic assassins attack break out their Ultimate Form. They can take on a Mothra form and carry the rest of their party on their back across the ocean without taking ever-increasing damage.<br /> <br /> So, to get to the level of a Solar warstrider pilot with 10 evocations, I expect you'll need 15 charms, because you've got the advantage of convenience and not having to invest in a bunch of Craft charms and 9 Merit dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I do expect that, even it requires more charms, you will be able to create a high-Essence Lunar that can challenge a Warstrider in Kaiju vs Mecha combat, if that's what you want to build. Not just for the look of it but because there's no way an Essence 5 Full Moon with 30 combat charms isn't a combatant of earth-shaking power. Considering how many charms were in the Solar and Dragonblood books, Lunars are going to have a ton of charms, and if, say, a quarter of them are combat charms, that'll be a hell of a lot of combat charms. And, like Solar combat charms and Warstriders, not all of them are going to be relevant to Kaiju combat (DBT upgrade charms aren't useful) but most of them will.<br /> It's not like they're going to put a &quot;Legendary Size - No&quot; keyword on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T12:28:00-08:00","id":1281342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281330#post1281330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect the Daikaiju charm tree to be big enough and go into high enough essence that you can become a Mythic Beast from the Primordial War if you get all of it</div> </div> </div> </div>If a daikaiju Charm tree is even a thing as such, I would expect it to be consistent within a wider Charm cascade.<br /> <br /> Deadly Beastman Transformation building off of and incorporating Hybrid Body Transformation is one thing, but the idea of trees of Charms locked behind a particular kind of transformation... it seems odd to me, especially when Protean Charms are there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect such creatures to be legitimately terrifying in similar ways to Warstriders</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrifying, sure; they\u2019re still Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> What qualifies as similar to a warstrider?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrillantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, I\u2019d want my ultimate E5 Daikaiju form to be at least somewhere on par with a Survival Supernal Solar\u2019s fully upgraded Familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, being basically unkillable?<br /> <br /> I think there are a few things those familiars can get that are a bit overpowered in a full-fledged character in their own right (especially one with a library of other powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T03:23:49-08:00","id":1281480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281338#post1281338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, to get to the level of a Solar warstrider pilot with 10 evocations, I expect you'll need 15 charms, because you've got the advantage of convenience and not having to invest in a bunch of Craft charms and 9 Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>13 dots. You need resources 4 to do most of that stuff.<br /> You don't usually pay xp for those merits over the course of the game, but damn if you don't need a ton of them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T01:53:59-08:00","id":1281625,"title":"","content":"In terms of a &quot;Daikaiju charm tree&quot; I don't think it needs to be that big. A couple of charms about being giant, the charm that cuts the cost, maybe a charm or two about smashing scenery.<br /> The real power is that, unlike a warstrider pilot, you can still use all your soak charms and strength-boosting charms while in giant size.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T05:46:46-08:00","id":1281637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281625#post1281625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real power is that, unlike a warstrider pilot, you can still use all your soak charms and strength-boosting charms while in giant size.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you? Has it been reported definitively that the boosts from turning giant don't count as dice added by Charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T07:34:32-08:00","id":1281640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281637#post1281637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you? Has it been reported definitively that the boosts from turning giant don't count as dice added by Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The last I heard on the discord everything a lunar gets counts as charm dice but I am not sure what &quot;everything&quot; entails, so maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T08:04:16-08:00","id":1281641,"title":"","content":"Strength is almost certainly capped because they've got charms to let you target attacks with it. Soak probably isn't unless they've introduced mechanics for a cap that they're retroactively applying to Solars and Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T15:12:26-08:00","id":1281700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281641#post1281641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength is almost certainly capped because they've got charms to let you target attacks with it. Soak probably isn't unless they've introduced mechanics for a cap that they're retroactively applying to Solars and Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cap would just be on Stamina.<br /> <br /> However, that raises the question to my mind of how stamina caps effect soak from your animal forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T16:03:43-08:00","id":1281708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281700#post1281700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cap would just be on Stamina.<br /> <br /> However, that raises the question to my mind of how stamina caps effect soak from your animal forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably it would just limit how much your can increase your natural soak up to the animals, like what dexterity does for the dice pools","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T16:28:44-08:00","id":1281714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281708#post1281708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably it would just limit how much your can increase your natural soak up to the animals, like what dexterity does for the dice pools</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, maybe, but considering you don't get your armor while transformed and QC pools aren't broken into 'natural' and 'armor' soak, you'd end up capping your soak at really low values while transformed. For an example, even a bear has soak 10 which would be capped at 5 normally or 10 with a stunt. Which means you need two traits at maximum <i>and </i>you need to stunt every time you want your soak above 5. Without stunting, someone with light armor is usually going to match or beat that, while someone with light artifact armor will <i>always</i> beat that.<br /> <br /> It also gives rise to the oddity that a lunar who transforms into an Armored Terror doesn't get much in the way of soak.<br /> <br /> Hell, consider a combat-focused lunar who hasn't maxed out stamina. It's hard to consider someone 'combat focused' when their soak is three.<br /> <br /> Edit: I later realized that I'd been borking the math here.the lunar's dice cap for natural soak would be their staminaX2. So a Stamina 2 lunar cap would be 4, or a stamina 3 lunar would be 6. So a stamina focused lunar still couldn't get full benefits from something like the Armored Terror (Soak 17) but with appropriate stats and a stunt could get pretty close (soak 15).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 01-20-2019, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T02:46:21-08:00","id":1281910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281640#post1281640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last I heard on the discord everything a lunar gets counts as charm dice but I am not sure what &amp;quot;everything&amp;quot; entails, so maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly my point.<br /> <br /> I'm sure the specifics will all be worked out in due time, but for the moment it can be agreed that turning giant does not allow you to ultimately push your stats higher than they would otherwise go; at best, it might make doing so more efficient.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it will be without advantages, but to just keep things in perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T03:49:47-08:00","id":1281918,"title":"","content":"If my Strength 4, Stamina 4 Lunar turns into, say, a Tyrant Lizard, what's their soak? 8 or 15?<br /> What's their Damage on a bite? Tyrant Lizards have 16. Is mine 11? 13? 15? It doesn't say if it's a Light, Medium or Heavy weapon after all.<br /> <br /> Currently, your attribute+ability dice pools are capped. But Stamina and Damage aren't attribute+ability dice pools.<br /> So my Strength 4, Brawl 3 Lunar rolls 11 dice to hit (like Tyrant Lizards) but can't increase it with excellencies. But their damage is 16, same as a tyrant lizard. And they could increase it with Damage charms that increase withering damage (though currently there aren't any).<br /> <br /> If you say Soak is capped at, say, 10 for a Stamina 5 Lunar, then Lunar giant animals are pretty flimsy, much flimsier than regular giant animals. They already have a lot less health levels after all, unless you take a ton of Ox-Bodies.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Stamina 4, Resistance 5, Essence 5 Solar can use Resistance charms to increase their soak by 29+. They can further increase it with Martial Arts charms.*<br /> But a Stamina 5 Lunar will only be able, with multiple charms, to increase it by 5?<br /> That seems a bit unfair.<br /> <br /> *Except in a Warstrider, where they can increase it by 0 using charms, of course.<br /> <br /> (The same applies to damage. With various Martial Arts charms combo'd, a Solar can increase their Withering damage by a lot. I haven't added up everything, but I've seen +15 extra damage with combo'd martial arts. It seems unfair to cap Lunars at +5 even if they have Strength 5).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, one dev (I forget who) did mention a long time ago that the Stamina and Strength excellency would have to be written in such a way as to address using them to increase damage or soak (currently, you technically can't use the excellencies to increase damage or soak at all). I'm sure that, if, for example, you can use the Strength excellency to boost damage (and I'm not sure if you will be able to), it will have some sort of internal cap*, but putting a hard limit of 5 or less on on all combos of damage and soak charms seems quite unfair considering both Solars and Dragonblood don't have a cap.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I can see the devs not wanting to see utterly abusable combos brought in. The fact you can't use Martial Arts charms or most Evocations in animal form helps with this, so they don't have to worry about people using the soak and damage increasing charms from Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> But they can do this by balancing the Lunars' own Strength and Stamina charmsets, rather than putting on a limit to Damage and Soak that's never applied before (in any edition) and doesn't apply to Solars or Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Someone mentioned that Lunars need a cap on Strength because of the charm that lets you attack with Strength. That already has a limit. Soak and Damage are not limited by excellency caps, Attacks are limited, because they're attribute+ability rolls, unlike damage. That's how it works for Solars, Dragonblood, and the way Excellencies are written up for Lunars in the Antagonist section of the Core book).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>Seperate</i> to being able to increase her Stamina rolls, Eska can increase her Soak using the excellency by the pretty measly limit of Stamina/2, or Stamina+Attribute/2 with a stunt. I don't believe that Lunars are only going to be able to increase their Soak by a max of 3 with any combination of their entire Stamina tree. Nor do I believe a Stamina 5 Lunar that turns into a 30 foot monster is going to be capped at a Soak of 8. I can and do believe that the Stamina excellency, in addition to letting you increase your Stamina rolls, also allows a Stamina 5 Lunar to increase their soak by 3, but I doubt 3 is the hard limit on soak increases for Lunars across the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-21-2019, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T05:35:42-08:00","id":1281930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281918#post1281918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you say Soak is capped at, say, 10 for a Stamina 5 Lunar, then Lunar giant animals are pretty flimsy</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be that they get to go above for the sake of getting the full power of those beings, but no further.<br /> <br /> What you were proposing before sounds way too far in the opposite direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Stamina 4, Resistance 5, Essence 5 Solar can use Resistance charms to increase their soak by 29+. They can further increase it with Martial Arts charms.*<br /> But a Stamina 5 Lunar will only be able, with multiple charms, to increase it by 5?<br /> That seems a bit unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may need to be the burden of Attribute Charms.<br /> <br /> How many motes does that 29 soak cost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T05:50:23-08:00","id":1281932,"title":"","content":"If Soaking n+1 damage and Wolverine style regeneration (and the ability to become a Three Storey Behemoth) are some of the things that Lunars have an edge on Solars in, you know what, I'm kind of okay with that.<br /> <br /> If we're to move away from the Silver Solars of 2nd ed, then yes, there has to be some differentiation, and while I grant that Solars should basically be better at all the application of skills than anyone else, Lunars should have the things they are superior at too, and what better choices than the very things they were known for since 1st edition?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-21-2019, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T07:19:23-08:00","id":1281939,"title":"","content":"Lunars will be able to boost their soak by anything the Devs feel is appropriate because there is no cap on <i><b>Soak</b></i>. The Stamina excellency may have a special call out for how it effects soak because your 'Natural Soak' is equal to your Stamina rating. My question was simply whether animals, being QC, interact with that cap in any way. Obviously the animals have higher soak than their Stamina, but we don't know by how much because they're QC.<br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I come to the conclusion that you'll probably just take the Soak rating directly from the animal you're shapeshifted in to. I imagine that soak boosting charms will only work on your characters own soak rating and then you could use that if it's better. Otherwise, being able to boost a soak of 17 (Armored Terror) by an additional 29 would be ridiculous. Since they want Lunars in their own form to be effective in combat, I doubt they'd nerf soak boosting charms to make it that much lower.<br /> <br /> Or maybe an armored terror lunar will be an un-hittable monstrosity. We'll find out I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T11:57:12-08:00","id":1281988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281918#post1281918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my Strength 4, Stamina 4 Lunar turns into, say, a Tyrant Lizard, what's their soak? 8 or 15?<br /> What's their Damage on a bite? Tyrant Lizards have 16. Is mine 11? 13? 15? It doesn't say if it's a Light, Medium or Heavy weapon after all.<br /> <br /> Currently, your attribute+ability dice pools are capped. But Stamina and Damage aren't attribute+ability dice pools.<br /> So my Strength 4, Brawl 3 Lunar rolls 11 dice to hit (like Tyrant Lizards) but can't increase it with excellencies. But their damage is 16, same as a tyrant lizard. And they could increase it with Damage charms that increase withering damage (though currently there aren't any).<br /> <br /> If you say Soak is capped at, say, 10 for a Stamina 5 Lunar, then Lunar giant animals are pretty flimsy, much flimsier than regular giant animals. They already have a lot less health levels after all, unless you take a ton of Ox-Bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure we've already been told how this is going to work. Lunar's have to obey dice caps just like everyone else, but their shape-shifting allows them to break those limits with certain stipulations. From what I remember of Vance's comment when you shape-shift into another critter, you get all that critters stats, even if they exceed your own dice caps. The caveat being if you exceed your dice caps, your then unable to alter those abilities via charms because you're already capped! Soak though, as you mention, is a bit of an oddball because it has an excellency cap for Lunar's due to their attribute-based charm set. My guess, is that while the Lunar's excellency to boost Soak has a limit, they can still stack other Soak boosting charms just like a Solar. So a Lunar in Tyrant Lizard form probably can't use his Stamina excellency to boost Soak, but will still be able to use normal charms to amplify Soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T14:03:11-08:00","id":1282008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1280838-what\u2019s-the-over-under-on-warstrider-solar-vs-daikaiju-lunar?p=1281988#post1281988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure we've already been told how this is going to work. Lunar's have to obey dice caps just like everyone else, but their shape-shifting allows them to break those limits with certain stipulations. From what I remember of Vance's comment when you shape-shift into another critter, <b>you get all that critters stats, even if they exceed your own dice caps</b>. The caveat being if you exceed your dice caps, your then unable to alter those abilities via charms because you're already capped! Soak though, as you mention, is a bit of an oddball because it has an excellency cap for Lunar's due to their attribute-based charm set. My guess, is that while the Lunar's excellency to boost Soak has a limit, they can still stack other Soak boosting charms just like a Solar. So a Lunar in Tyrant Lizard form probably can't use his Stamina excellency to boost Soak, but will still be able to use normal charms to amplify Soak.</div> </div> </div> </div>No you explicitly do not.<br /> <br /> If you have Strength 2, Athletics 1 and you turn into a Tyrant Lizard and want to perform a feat of strength, you only get 5 dice (str 2+Ath 1 + str 2). If you stunt it in such a way as you can bring your stamina to bear then you can also add it to the cap. So if you've got stamina 5, you could potentially have a feats of strength pool of 10 in such a case. You don't have to spend motes, but you do NOT get the full 12 dice unless you have the stats to support it.<br /> <br /> Found the relevant quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1176078#post1176078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Current model is that you use the better of your own (Attribute + Ability) or an animal form's dice pools. If it's an animal form's, then any dice over your natural amount count as Charm dice.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1178330#post1178330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting doesn't let a Lunar reach a dice pool higher than the maxed-out dice limit they'd have in human form, by any means.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":8804,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","user":"armyofwhispers","date":". 01-21-2019, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}